== tb_vpu_latency_probe
 vpu architectural latency probe
 L = cycles from producer ISSUE to the earliest consumer ISSUE
     that observes the new value.
===============================================================

  vld   -> V-slot consumer     L = 7   (docs/isa_latency.json: W + 1)
  vadd  -> V-slot consumer     L = 6   (docs/isa_latency.json: W + 1)
  vld   -> X-slot vst          L = 7   (docs/isa_latency.json: W + 1)
  vgelu -> V-slot consumer     L = 8   (docs/isa_latency.json: W + 1)
  vlanesum -> V-slot consumer  L = 12   (docs/isa_latency.json: W + 1)
  vtxout   -> V-slot consumer  L = 4   (docs/isa_latency.json: W + 1)
  vredsum  -> V-slot consumer  L = 16   (docs/isa_latency.json: W + 1)

 A consumer issued at producer_issue + L sees the new value;
 a direct datapath consumer at + (L-1) sees the stale one.
 Nothing holds such a bundle: the schedule must space it.
 Both the V slot's operand registers and the X slot's
 store-data path sample the VREG file combinationally at issue,
 so one L covers both consumer kinds.
